Dear Developers<div><br></div><div>We are currently looking to combine phospho analysis of DDA data using FragPipe and MSstatsPTM.</div><div><br></div><div>I have noticed that there is a nice converter tool:</div><div><br></div><div>MSstatsPTM::FragPipetoMSstatsPTMFormat</div><div><br></div><div>Which states in the description:<br><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px"><span style="font-size:10pt"><br>input</span><span style="font-size:10pt"><br></span></span><span style="font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif">data.frame of</span><span style="font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif">msstats.csv</span><span style="font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif"> </span><span style="font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif">file produced by Philosopher</span> </div><div><br></div><div>which looks like this:</div><div><br></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="color:rgb(200,0,164)">&gt; </span><span style="color:rgb(200,0,164)">PO %&gt;% colnames()
</span><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"> [1] &quot;ProteinName&quot;      &quot;PeptideSequence&quot;  &quot;PrecursorCharge&quot;  &quot;FragmentIon&quot;     
 [5] &quot;ProductCharge&quot;    &quot;IsotopeLabelType&quot; &quot;Condition&quot;        &quot;BioReplicate&quot;    
 [9] &quot;Run&quot;              &quot;Intensity&quot;    </span></span></span><br></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px">when I tried to run the converter it (rightfully) complained that I forgot to specify the FASTA file. However, how can I specify the fasta file in the converter? This argument seems to be missing (I would expect something like fasta_path).</span></span></span></div><div><span aria-label="Console Output" role="document" style="font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0)"><span role="document" style="outline:none"><span style="outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px"><br></span></span></span></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">Also does not work to provide a workaround with &quot;Start&quot; column in the msstats.csv output of philospher. The converter still wants to have a fasta AND complains that the Start column is missing.</span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">Additionally, I found the argument </span></font></div><div><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt"><br>localization_cutoff</span><span style="color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt"><br><p style="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px">Minimum localization score required to keep modification. Default is .75.</p></span></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">somewhat confusing as the output of philosopher does not contain any site confidence score.</span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">If you need a small reproducible example I would be happy to provide one for you, but I think I must have a different input than whoever wrote the adapter?</span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">I am using the msstats.csv file generated by FragPipe upon activating the msstats.csv output in the VALIDATION tab. It is then generated in the overall experiment folder of the FragPipe search. Is this the correct output?</span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px">Best, Klemens</span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div><div><font color="#000000" face="Lucida Console, monospace"><span style="font-size:13.3333px"><br></span></font></div>
